WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:02.210
Let's talk about Dr.

00:00:02.210 --> 00:00:03.210
Anthony Foushee.

00:00:03.210 --> 00:00:08.901
Dr. Anthony Foushee has to be very careful
in his role on the White House Coronavirus

00:00:08.901 --> 00:00:13.380
Task Force, in his role as the top infectious
disease doctor in the United States.

00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:14.380
He's always there.

00:00:14.380 --> 00:00:15.380
He's on TV.

00:00:15.380 --> 00:00:16.609
He's at many of Trump's press briefings.

00:00:16.609 --> 00:00:18.470
He's being interviewed all the time.

00:00:18.470 --> 00:00:24.839
And he is an actual doctor, meaning that the
things he says are typically true when they're

00:00:24.839 --> 00:00:29.909
within his area of expertise, which is infectious
disease that is very different than Donald

00:00:29.909 --> 00:00:30.909
Trump.

00:00:30.909 --> 00:00:35.660
But when Foushee was asked in an interview
a few weeks ago, why aren't you publicly contradicting

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:38.030
Trump when he tells his lies?

00:00:38.030 --> 00:00:40.530
Foushee essentially said, This is my paraphrase.

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:44.700
Foushee said, You know, it's not realistic
for me to step in front of him at the podium

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:47.739
every time he says something that's wrong
and say, no, no, no.

00:00:47.739 --> 00:00:49.059
And it sort of seems

00:00:49.059 --> 00:00:54.510
like Foushee recognizes that his presence
is more important than contradicting Trump

00:00:54.510 --> 00:00:55.660
at every opportunity.

00:00:55.660 --> 00:01:00.519
And we've even seen Foushee in some moments
express exasperation visibly.

00:01:00.519 --> 00:01:06.299
One of those moments was when Donald Trump
mentioned the deep state during a press briefing

00:01:06.299 --> 00:01:12.520
and Dr. Foushee literally face palmed, incredulous
about what Donald Trump was saying at a more

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:13.650
recent press conference.

00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:16.200
Dr. Foushee was directly asked.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:19.010
Here's what the president says about hydroxy
chloroquine.

00:01:19.010 --> 00:01:20.990
Can you comment about it?

00:01:20.990 --> 00:01:27.399
And Trump literally did not allow Dr. Foushee
to answer the question, and Foushee looked

00:01:27.399 --> 00:01:29.220
very uncomfortable.

00:01:29.220 --> 00:01:35.040
But finally, Dr Foushee has made it clear
that were it not for Donald Trump's actions,

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:38.030
we might have been able to save people.

00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:43.820
And Donald Trump is immediately signaling
that he may be preparing to fire Dr. Foushee.

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:45.430
Let's go through it step by step.

00:01:45.430 --> 00:01:46.549
This is from CNN.

00:01:46.549 --> 00:01:47.750
Now, remember, we have

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:51.940
to have realistic expectations about what
Anthony Foushee will say about he's not going

00:01:51.940 --> 00:01:53.049
to insult Trump.

00:01:53.049 --> 00:01:55.289
He's not going to say Trump failed us.

00:01:55.289 --> 00:02:00.579
But Dr. Foushee admitted and this is something
that they've not yet been clear about.

00:02:00.579 --> 00:02:08.759
Dr. Foushee admits if we had taken this more
seriously earlier, we would have saved lives.

00:02:08.759 --> 00:02:11.500
Take a look at the video from CNN.

00:02:11.500 --> 00:02:16.060
The New York Times reported yesterday that
you and other top officials wanted to recommend

00:02:16.060 --> 00:02:19.620
social and physical distancing guidelines
to President Trump.

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:21.599
As far back as the third week of February.

00:02:21.599 --> 00:02:25.989
But the administration didn't announce such
guidelines to the American public until March

00:02:25.989 --> 00:02:28.680
16th, almost a month later.

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:36.330
You know, Jake, as I've said many times, we
look at it from a pure health standpoint.

00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:37.860
We make a recommendation.

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:39.910
Often the recommendation is taken.

00:02:39.910 --> 00:02:41.480
Sometimes it's not.

00:02:41.480 --> 00:02:42.819
But we it is what it is.

00:02:42.819 --> 00:02:45.540
We are where we are right now.

00:02:45.540 --> 00:02:52.690
Do you think lives could have been saved if
social distancing, physical distancing?

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:54.650
Stay at home measures had started.

00:02:54.650 --> 00:02:56.160
Third week of February instead of mid-March.

00:02:56.160 --> 00:03:02.940
Jake, again, it's the what would have what
could have.

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:04.940
It's very difficult to to go back and say
that.

00:03:04.940 --> 00:03:10.390
I mean, obviously, you could logically say
that if you had a process that was ongoing

00:03:10.390 --> 00:03:13.989
and you started mitigation earlier, you could
have saved lives.

00:03:13.989 --> 00:03:16.310
Obviously, no one is going to deny that.

00:03:16.310 --> 00:03:19.560
But what goes into those kinds of decisions
is complicated.

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:20.560
But you're right.

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:25.160
I mean, obviously, if we add right from the
very beginning, shut everything down, it may

00:03:25.160 --> 00:03:28.909
have been a little bit different, but there
was a lot of pushback about shutting things

00:03:28.909 --> 00:03:30.330
down back then.

00:03:30.330 --> 00:03:32.010
Do you think lives could have been saved?

00:03:32.010 --> 00:03:33.890
Yes, they could have been it.

00:03:33.890 --> 00:03:35.030
Dr. Foushee.

00:03:35.030 --> 00:03:37.650
He uses non-confrontational language.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:42.390
But this is a big deal because Donald Trump
has been insisting and continues to insist

00:03:42.390 --> 00:03:44.770
there was nothing he could possibly have done
differently.

00:03:44.770 --> 00:03:47.569
There was nothing he could possibly have done
earlier.

00:03:47.569 --> 00:03:50.379
No matter what he had known, had he read those
memos?

00:03:50.379 --> 00:03:52.580
He didn't read no matter what.

00:03:52.580 --> 00:03:53.580
He did everything.

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:56.680
As soon as it could have been done and nothing
could have been done differently.

00:03:56.680 --> 00:04:01.460
Trump has denied the notion that if he had
acted earlier, lives would have been saved.

00:04:01.460 --> 00:04:05.780
Despite the reality that, you know, you don't
really need to be a doctor to realize that

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:07.010
that's not true.

00:04:07.010 --> 00:04:11.370
Also important was that Anthony Foushee said
we make recommendations.

00:04:11.370 --> 00:04:16.360
The recommendations are always taken for Anthony
Fouty's temperament.

00:04:16.360 --> 00:04:18.120
That is him saying, we told

00:04:18.120 --> 00:04:20.340
Trump and he ignored us.

00:04:20.340 --> 00:04:23.230
We can't expect Dr. Foushee to make direct
attacks.

00:04:23.230 --> 00:04:26.130
We can't expect him to behave like Trump does.

00:04:26.130 --> 00:04:29.280
But this is a doctor making it clear recommendations
were made.

00:04:29.280 --> 00:04:30.450
They were not followed.

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:33.150
If they had been followed, we would have fewer
deaths right now.

00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:36.580
But remember, on a per capita basis, it's
not even close.

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:40.570
In South Korea, South Korea's population is
smaller than ours.

00:04:40.570 --> 00:04:45.130
But importantly, both countries had their
first cases right around February 20th.

00:04:45.130 --> 00:04:47.390
Matter of hours separating the two.

00:04:47.390 --> 00:04:52.790
On a per capita basis, our case rate is seventeen
hundred cases per million.

00:04:52.790 --> 00:04:54.290
Theirs is two hundred and five.

00:04:54.290 --> 00:04:55.860
That's not an error.

00:04:55.860 --> 00:04:57.950
Seventeen hundred versus 2 0 5.

00:04:57.950 --> 00:05:02.450
As Dr. Foushee says, the heterogeneity of
the population may be a factor.

00:05:02.450 --> 00:05:05.250
Doesn't explain a 9 X difference.

00:05:05.250 --> 00:05:06.420
Moving early does.

00:05:06.420 --> 00:05:07.920
And they moved early.

00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:09.840
Our test rate is eighty

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:11.040
five hundred per million.

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:13.040
There is this ten thousand per million.

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:16.370
We have a 20 percent lower test rate.

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:21.070
And of course, that's now bearing in mind
that they were that high much, much earlier.

00:05:21.070 --> 00:05:23.080
And it's reflected in the death toll.

00:05:23.080 --> 00:05:25.940
Our death rate is 67 per million.

00:05:25.940 --> 00:05:27.500
South Korea's is four.

00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:29.430
That's not an error.

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:32.310
Their death rate is four people per million.

00:05:32.310 --> 00:05:33.500
Ours is 67.

00:05:33.500 --> 00:05:38.610
Our death rate is almost 17 times higher than
South Korea's.

00:05:38.610 --> 00:05:45.350
Now, unfortunately, Trump appears to be signaling
he may be ready to fire Dr. Foushee after

00:05:45.350 --> 00:05:47.420
this statement came out yesterday from Dr.
Foushee.

00:05:47.420 --> 00:05:49.800
If we had moved earlier, we could have saved
people.

00:05:49.800 --> 00:05:55.960
Trump retweeted a tweet from a lady named
Diane Laraine who said Foushee is now saying

00:05:55.960 --> 00:06:00.410
that had Trump listened to the medical experts
earlier, he could have saved more lives.

00:06:00.410 --> 00:06:02.510
She was telling people on February

00:06:02.510 --> 00:06:08.550
29 that there was nothing to worry about and
it posed no threat to the U.S. public at large.

00:06:08.550 --> 00:06:15.650
Time to fire Foushee Trump re-tweeting that
and adding that it is all fake news.

00:06:15.650 --> 00:06:20.170
There is very clearly little tolerance for
dissension in the ranks.

00:06:20.170 --> 00:06:23.730
It seems Dr. Foushee may soon be fired by
Donald Trump.

00:06:23.730 --> 00:06:26.360
I hope it doesn't happen if we do do it.

00:06:26.360 --> 00:06:27.710
If we do lose Dr. Foushee.

00:06:27.710 --> 00:06:29.780
It is going to get even worse.

00:06:29.780 --> 00:06:34.860
We will see if Dr. Foushee is there today
at the White House coronavirus press briefing,

00:06:34.860 --> 00:06:37.070
but it is not looking good.

